Jo Thueson, played by Ann Hearn.

9
00:37:57,391 --> 00:38:03,391
Noah, played by Jim Byrnes.

10
00:42:10,434 --> 00:42:16,434
Omen IV: The Awakening is a 1991 American supernatural horror television film directed by Jorge Montesi and Dominique
Othenin-Girard and written by Brian Taggert, from a story by producer Harvey Bernhard and Taggert.

11
00:46:23,478 --> 00:46:29,478
The film is the fourth installment in The Omen franchise and
the final installment of the original franchise.

12
00:50:36,521 --> 00:50:42,521
It stars Faye Grant, Michael Woods, Michael Lerner, and Asia Vieira.

13
00:54:49,565 --> 00:54:55,565
Its plot follows two attorneys who adopt a young girl, unaware of the fact
that she is to possibly succeed Damien Thorn as the Antichrist.

14
00:59:02,608 --> 00:59:08,608
The film was intended to be the first of many television sequels to
20th Century Fox's film history of popular titles.

15
01:03:15,652 --> 01:03:21,652
Bernhard, who also produced the previous three Omen films,
felt there could be more done to the series.

16
01:07:28,695 --> 01:07:34,695
This was the last film he produced.

17
01:11:41,739 --> 01:11:47,739
He previously wrote the story for the second film.

18
01:15:54,782 --> 01:16:00,782
Omen IV: The Awakening premiered on television in North
America on the Fox network, on May 20, 1991.

19
01:20:07,826 --> 01:20:13,826
The film was given a theatrical release in some countries, such as Australia, where it premiered on
August 9, 1991, and in the United Kingdom, where it opened on November 29, 1991.

20
01:24:20,869 --> 01:24:26,869
It was largely panned by critics upon release.

21
01:28:33,913 --> 01:28:39,913
The film explores themes of prophecy, politics,
anti-christ, evil child, mysterious death.

22
01:32:46,956 --> 01:32:52,956
The tone is intense and dark and mind_bending.
